  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Math Functions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "There is also a list of math functions available, that allows you to perform mathematical tasks on numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "To use them, you must include the `math.h` **header file** in your program:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  #include <math.h>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Square Root",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "To find the square root of a number, use the `sqrt()` function:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  printf(\"%f\", sqrt(16));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Round a Number",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "The `ceil()` function rounds a number upwards to its nearest integer, and the `floor()` method rounds a number downwards to its nearest integer, and returns the result:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  printf(\"%f\", ceil(1.4));\nprintf(\"%f\", \n  floor(1.4));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Power",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "The `pow()` function returns the value of *x* to the power of *y* (*xy*):"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "content": "  printf(\"%f\", pow(4, 3));"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Complete Math Reference",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "content": "For a complete reference of math functions, go to our C <math.h> Library Reference."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
